WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.810
Dive into the ocean, and
the light fades fast.

2
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:08.910
Below 200 metres, so little light gets
through that photosynthesis is no longer

3
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:09.990
possible.

4
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.810
Below 1,000 metres, there
is no sunlight at all.

5
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.510
The water is cold and steady.

6
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.530
Further down lies the abyssal plain,
about 70 per cent of the ocean floor.

7
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.530
And life is found there.

8
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.670
No sunlight, no plants.

9
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.430
So how does anything live in the deep?

10
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.990
Or is it simply empty?

11
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:34.510
In this mission, you'll see how light,
temperature and nutrients change with depth

12
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.190
and with latitude.

13
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.830
Then you'll compare the food web of a
rocky shore with the life far below.

14
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.480
Your mission: find out how life
survives in the dark of the deep ocean.
